1. How do I use the melt function to reshape my data frame?  Do I need to add some sort of “subject,”, and if so, what would that look like?

2. Once the data frame is reshaped, what command would facet the four plots?  (I'd like only the bottom one to have dates shown on the x axis.)

Thank you for any help.
David  Here's the code:

date = 33817:34303   ## My actual dates
y1 = runif(487,0,5)
y2 = rnorm(487,100,30)
y3 = runif(487,0,1000)
y4 = runif(487,0,100)
df = data.frame(y1,y2,y3,y4,date)
library(ggplot2)
library(reshape2)
ggplot(df, aes(x=date, y=y1)) + geom_point()
ggplot(df, aes(x=date, y=y2)) + geom_point()
ggplot(df, aes(x=date, y=y3)) + geom_point()
ggplot(df, aes(x=date, y=y4)) + geom_point()

