That's strange, because other annotations work, e.g.
zz+annotate("point",x=as.POSIXct("2014-02-16"),y=50)

Going through the call stack, it looks like the error ("'/' not
defined for "POSIXt" objects") occurs in scales::rescale, when a date
(x-from[1]) gets divided by a numeric (diff(from)). Unless someone
chimes in with a better idea, I'd file a bug report at
https://github.com/hadley/scales/issues.

Ben

